WEBVTT

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:46.290
Yo.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.080
Morning, Toki.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.380
Good morning.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.380
Sorry to ask you so suddenly,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.630
but I've just found out that
a difficult guest is coming today.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.970
Could you hide out at Kon's
place for a little while?

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.510
You have a guest?

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.480
No problem.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.350
Oh?

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.270
What's this?

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.060
My, it looks like a fancy eyepatch.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.310
Ah, this?

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.610
One of Shinonome's neighbors made it for me.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.780
Oh?

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.780
It's quite stylish.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.320
They seem to be taking good care of you.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.330
I'm glad you've been able to open up to others.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:30.170
Life is short, and it passes
in the blink of an eye.

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.250
Don't be led astray because one eye is sealed.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:36.590
Observe the world with an open heart,
and you'll find happiness and good fortune.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.090
Remember that, Toki.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:41.260
Sure.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:06.160
What do you think, Oume-san?

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:06.990
Does it suit me?

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.830
Hm, well.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:12.040
I think you look a bit better than before.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.840
I'm glad to hear that!

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.220
I'd guess it's thanks to your skills.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.220
You really know what to say
to make a person happy.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.890
Toki-san, look at these.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.180
They look delicious!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.390
May I have one?

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.100
Yes, of course.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.520
I made them just for you, Toki-san.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:35.230
Thanks for the food!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.110
Tasty!

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.110
Your cooking gets better every time.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:41.860
Really?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.320
You know, Toki-chan, I've got some dumplings at my house as well.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.030
Should I bring them for you?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:47.910
Would you?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.620
Great!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.250
In that case, I'd like to share some with my friends as well.

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.290
Say, why don't we all have tea together?

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:58.130
But I made these especially for you, Toki-san.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:02.300
I feel like I'll be punished if I keep all your delicious food to myself.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.890
You silver-tongued devil!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.760
What is that?

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.680
Man, I envy him. Damn!

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.850
Heihachi-san, Shinonome.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.640
Let's go for tea together.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.560
They've all brought snacks for us.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.020
Seriously?!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.400
Th-This is a time for a man
to prove his worth.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.650
Wait for me!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.070
I'm going to bring some sweets
from the store as well!

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:27.530
You've settled in nicely.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.290
Where did that come from?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.080
Did you make it yourself?

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.330
It was given to me yesterday.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.710
Oume-san made it for me.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.630
She also adjusted the size properly,

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.460
so it won't fall off like the old one.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.800
This will let me keep it hidden.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:43.720
I see.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.590
Hey! W-Wait!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.550
These snacks aren't for you.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.100
Don't pull that!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.600
Don't hang on to that.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.400
But if Oume did that much for you,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.110
she probably thinks of you as a kid.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.110
As a kid, huh?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.030
What's up, Toki?

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:11.740
I was just thinking that nobody's ever been so nice to me before.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.050
Sorry, did I say something strange?

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.250
No, not at all.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.790
It's nothing, nothing.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.260
I'll wash my hands before we go for tea.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.180
That wasn't like me...

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.260
getting upset about something like that.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.940
I have found you, sir.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.150
I was looking for the fiery chariot.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.770
Surely, surely.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:44.940
But instead, I found Momotarou,

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:48.160
the child of the gods who defeated the gods.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.490
However, however, it doesn't end there.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:54.870
This fellow's true identity

00:05:54.870 --> 00:06:00.000
could even be said to be Shuten Douji.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.170
Douji loved his mother

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.340
and hated his father,
who had abandoned him.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.970
Yearning and yearning,

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.600
he missed his mother.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.770
This yearning for his mother
made the child into a demon.

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:16.020
That song!

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:16.850
Stop it!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:18.560
Surely, surely.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.150
That pitiable child.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.770
He is a pitiable child.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.270
Surely, surely.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.570
Pitiable child,

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.030
pitiful,

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.450
pitiful.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.420
Well, well.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:47.630
Isn't this an adorable little thing I've found?

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.800
Although that folk song
about Shuten Douji seems

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.760
to indicate another person
with prophetic powers.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.770
Hey, Tadajiro.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.770
You've been using the bathroom for ages—

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.190
Hey, Toki!

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.780
What are you doing here?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.280
It's about a little something
I borrowed from the Divine Princess.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.780
I'm done for.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.880
The tea here is the same as always.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:30.340
Well, I'm sorry about that.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.180
I'm sure it's very different from the tea
supplied to the Shogunate.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.930
Well, it's not bad, as a change.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.900
Well then, I'll get straight to the point.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:48.980
There were rumors that a demon
appeared around here the other day.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.530
Do you know about it?

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:55.370
The victim just happened
to come to me for help.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:58.080
The fellow seemed to be
terrified out of his wits,

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.120
so I couldn't just ignore him.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:05.920
Even though I consulted the man who should be best informed about these things,

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.420
he insisted that he didn't know anything.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.130
And so, there was nothing left to do
but use my secret weapon.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.470
And when I did, I caught you.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.390
Could you be the rumored demon?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:19.310
How dare you!

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.810
Does the boy look like a spirit?

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.100
Well, of course he doesn't.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.310
Then accept that you were
misinformed and give up.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.110
Who are you?

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.950
Ah, where are my manners?

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.320
I am known as Sasaki Tadajiro.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:40.240
My elder brother is Teshirogi Suguemon.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.660
My younger brother is Sasaki Tadasaburou.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.250
We are from Aizu Prefecture.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:48.590
You should know that we brothers are very loyal to each other.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.300
Some pretty influential names are being dropped around here again.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.800
Oh? Have you heard of me?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.850
No, but I've heard of your brothers.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:02.060
I see.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:03.890
Well, I suppose that's to be expected.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:05.810
My elder brother works with the government,

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.360
to protect the Shogunate
as the official face of Aizu Prefecture.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.820
My younger brother works
in the shadows with the military,

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.070
to protect the Shogunate and its leaders.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.650
And I stand in the shadows of the shadows.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.950
I protect Edo from unwanted things.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:20.660
I am a demon hunter, vital to the Shogunate.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.580
A demon hunter?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.750
For the Shogunate?

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.620
This is the first I've heard of it.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.370
Is there really a position like that?

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:30.880
It's not a job you'd be likely
to encounter on the streets.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.670
Hey, who is this guy?

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.800
I don't really know myself,

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.350
but there's a theory that his younger brother assassinated Sakamoto Ryouma.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:47.270
To be honest, I never expected matters would go this far.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.610
Even so, there was no need for you
to come investigate in person.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.030
Well, work is work,

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:56.780
and besides, I wanted to meet
my old friend, Shamon.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.110
This is bad.

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.830
Given our relative standing, we can't defy him.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:03.740
But I'm a normal human being.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.540
No matter what he tries
on me, it won't work.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.090
But we've got to keep
Kuchiha's secret hidden.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.960
We don't know what they'll say next.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.760
Also, we weren't completely blameless,

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.970
even if it wasn't much of a crime.

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:23.970
This era puts social status before justice.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.180
Those guys were samurai.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:29.350
Do you think we have any chance of winning,
as outsiders in this world?

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.610
But they don't have any proof against us.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.400
We'll be all right if we keep quiet.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.030
It will work out.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:38.990
I'll do something about it.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.160
It's not unusual for all those involved
to be put to death.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.420
I'm sorry!

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.090
I did it!

00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.130
I did it all myself.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.380
I'm so sorry!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.630
Wh-Wha— You idiot! What are you saying?!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.340
These guys had nothing to do with it.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.050
<i>What </i>am<i> I saying?</i>

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.760
I thought it up myself and put the plan into action.
<i>This could get me killed!</i>

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.890
<i>But I mustn't cause them
more problems than I already have.</i>

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.480
Hey, Toki!

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.020
My, my, it's most convenient
that you've confessed.

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.860
Well then, I suppose you
will have to be punished.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.110
This is all exactly what I deserve.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.030
Hey, wait a minute!

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.740
Your sentence is three days of babysitting!

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.750
It's a lot of hard work,

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.790
so you'd better think about
what you've done.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.500
I heard some thugs saying,

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:40.010
"They're keeping demons in that temple,"

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.850
so I thought I'd come by to check it out.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.390
But they were just blowing
smoke out their asses.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.270
I'm glad.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.150
Just relax.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:56.610
Despite appearances,
I've got a good eye for people.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.610
Between you and the "victim" in the case,

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:02.860
it's not hard to decide
who's more trustworthy.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.200
So, Tokidoki-kun,

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.370
you're supposed to be the culprit,

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.870
but after talking to you and examining you,

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.380
you seem to be an extremely normal boy.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.040
Despite that,

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.170
I still find it strange that the monster

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:24.720
could manipulate fire well enough to convince people it was real.

00:12:26.010 --> 00:12:29.810
That was just stuff I learned
in science and chemistry class.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.770
Science? Chemistry?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:34.060
No, um, I mean—

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.730
It's knowledge from the West.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.480
You're an educated fellow, Tokidoki-kun.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.900
Given how you look,

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.070
could you be a student from abroad?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.370
No, um, well...

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:50.490
Tadajiro!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.330
All right, all right.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.000
About the babysitting I mentioned before,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:00.050
I'll come by in three days' time to pick you up.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.800
Ah, sure.

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.590
Is something the matter?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.720
Nothing in particular.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.890
Then I'll see you in three days' time.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.390
It comes.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.230
Princess?

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:18.150
It is pure white.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:22.480
Finally... Finally the Princess has spoken!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:27.950
Prepare yourself, for events are coming
that even I cannot foresee.

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.070
No.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:29.990
Perhaps...

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.370
that is up to the gods.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.250
So the Princess has found him.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.330
Is he the enemy of this world,

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.380
or is he the complete opposite?

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.960
Only the gods themselves know the answer.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:49.300
Good work back there.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.140
Uh, I'm really sorry!

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:52.600
I thought he was with the police!

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.730
It's all in the past now.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:57.690
And besides, it worked out and
wasn't considered a serious crime.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:00.110
All's well that ends well.

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:07.780
Well, Shinonome warned me about it before,

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:12.910
but I guess I hadn't really understood what he was trying to tell me.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:21.000
Before I came here, my actions never had such huge effects on people around me.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.420
In Zen...

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.460
we have a commonly held belief.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.670
It's almost a "universal truth."

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.430
"Humans always look too deeply into the answers before them

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.760
and lose sight of them."

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.890
Or so it's said.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.140
When you were in your world,

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.520
even if you simply threw a pebble,

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.650
it should've changed the shape of the world.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.150
But those changes were so mundane and ordinary

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.360
that you simply didn't notice them.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.280
If you've started to see it now, Toki,

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.200
then it means your way of seeing
the world has changed.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.170
It all depends on your heart.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.210
Depends on... my heart—

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:06.710
Ow! What the hell was that for?!

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:07.880
You moron!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.560
I guess he felt you still
needed to be punished.

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.930
I see.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.850
He was worried about me.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:25.770
When did he become such a caring person?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:27.070
Toki...

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:31.070
That's another consequence
of a pebble you've thrown.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.910
I'll be on my way then.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:42.460
All right, take care on your journey.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.390
The weather's good today too.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.220
I hope you have an easy journey.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:57.850
Yes, then I'll be leaving.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:05.440
Hey, you've brought your sword with you?

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.610
Man, that's dangerous.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.150
It's just a precaution.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.400
Anything could happen.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.700
Oh?

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.570
Are you two coming as well?

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.820
What for?

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.780
Sasaki-san only asked me to come.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:22.540
I-I'm just here to make sure you don't go running off somewhere.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:23.460
That's it exactly.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:26.340
As if we could let a troublesome guy like you do whatever you liked.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.090
Also, I have a message from Heihachi.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.510
Oh.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:34.380
I'd assumed Shamon-san
asked you to do this.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:35.340
Am I wrong?

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:38.350
I could have used that.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.720
No, I...

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.940
I chose to do this myself!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.100
Got a problem with that?!

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:45.770
What the hell?!

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.110
Don't take it out on me!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.110
I used to have a lot of friends.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:53.990
This is great.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.740
To be honest, I would've
been lonely by myself.

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:58.410
Let go of me, you idiot!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.410
Don't touch me whenever you feel like it.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:02.500
We got along well and never fought.
Even if she's with you,

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.710
We liked each other.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:07.170
I thought that was how it was supposed to be.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.630
Yet...

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.920
I'm happier over here.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.300
So what was Heihachi's message?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.300
I'll tell you later.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.020
Hey, Kuchiha.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.520
This road...

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.770
Yeah. It has a menacing aura.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:31.400
Damn that old man. Where was he planning to take Toki?

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:35.030
He might be suspicious,
but he's not a bad guy.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.160
He's an acquaintance of Shamon-san, after all.

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.320
And that makes it okay?

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:40.910
Man.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.620
I keep telling you guys
that you worry too much.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.090
I hope this isn't a bad omen.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:57.680
Let's go.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:04.470
Toki, do you feel more at ease when you wear the eyepatch, or when you don't?

00:18:05.890 --> 00:18:07.310
Well,

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.900
I can't see spirits with the eyepatch,
so I'm more at ease that way.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:14.400
In other words, you don't feel awkward even with one eye covered?

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.900
Well, that's odd.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.410
Don't look, Toki.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.000
If you stare too much,
you'll get sucked in.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.500
This is a spirit road.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:37.050
If you lose your way,
you'll never be able to return.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.260
I've heard it's the road between
this world and the next.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.430
If you don't want to be lost,

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.520
keep your eyes on the road
and walk straight ahead.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.270
Kuchiha,

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.350
you look pale.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.820
I'm not very fond of places like this.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:55.030
Kuchiha!

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.070
I'm fine!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.400
It's nothing.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:01.070
This has nothing to do with you.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.040
I understand.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.040
You can make it.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:19.010
I'd like to take a little break.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.880
Yeah, I hear you.

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.550
I feel fine.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:26.810
I really don't feel fine.

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:30.560
Don't underestimate the strength of women from this era.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.810
Don't give up, don't give up.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:47.290
I guess this means we have
to keep going on our own.

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:48.750
It seems that way.

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:51.960
We've been walking for
more than two hours now,

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.330
and the destination still isn't in sight.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.000
Isn't that strange?

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:59.010
Maybe we're being misled on purpose.

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.170
On purpose?

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:03.680
They have some nerve, summoning people and then treating them like this.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:07.010
Are we supposed to figure out
which of these three paths is the right one?

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.350
Is he playing games with us?

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:15.520
What is it, Toki?

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:18.400
Just now, I saw something
that looked like a feather.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.570
A feather?

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.860
Was it a demon?

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:24.160
Um, I don't really know.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.700
I don't really know if it was a feather or not.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:29.830
It's this way!

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.000
What is it, Toki?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:32.210
Follow me!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.460
I see the path!

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.680
If you run when you're tired,
you'll fall down.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.760
I'm fine!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.980
Huh?

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.150
What happened?

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.110
Toki?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.160
What is this place?

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.960
What's happening here?

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.830
Are those two all right?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.430
I guess this is the bottom.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.640
I'm glad you made it here.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.480
I've been waiting for you.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.690
Now, let me ask you something.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.820
The fate of this world will be determined

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.650
through one simple question.
